<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/head', { pageTitle: 'Privacy Policy | Sutton Security Systems', pageDesc: 'How Sutton Security Systems collects, uses and protects your personal information.' }) %>
</head>
<body class="bg-white">
  <%- include('partials/header') %>

  <main>
    <section class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-black/5">
      <div class="container-x py-12">
        <span class="eyebrow text-brand mb-3">Legal</span>
        <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-soft text-sm">Last updated: July 2026</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-14">
      <div class="container-x max-w-3xl space-y-8 text-slate-soft leading-relaxed text-[15px]">

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">1. Who we are</h2>
          <p>Sutton Security Systems ("we", "us", "our") is a trading name of R &amp; U Services Limited. We supply and install wireless Ajax alarm systems for homes across the United Kingdom. We are the data controller for the personal information described in this policy. If you have any question about how your data is handled, contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@suttonss.co.uk" class="text-brand underline">contact@suttonss.co.uk</a> or on 07404 636800.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">2. The information we collect</h2>
          <p>We collect information you give us directly when you request a quote, book a survey, contact us or sign up for updates. This may include your name, phone number, email address, postcode and address, details about your property such as its type and number of bedrooms, and any information you choose to share about your security needs. If you contact us by phone, email or WhatsApp we keep a record of that correspondence.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">3. How we use your information</h2>
          <p>We use your information to respond to enquiries and provide quotes, to arrange surveys and installations, to provide ongoing support for your system, to keep records of the work we have carried out, and, where you have agreed, to send you occasional security tips and product news. We do not sell your personal information to anyone.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">4. Our legal bases</h2>
          <p>We process your data where it is necessary to take steps at your request before entering into a contract and to perform that contract, where we have a legitimate interest in running and promoting our business in a way you would reasonably expect, where you have given consent, for example to receive marketing emails, and where we need to comply with a legal obligation.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">5. Who we share it with</h2>
          <p>We share information only where needed to run our business: with Ajax Systems where required to register or support your equipment and its warranty, with service providers who help us operate, such as email and messaging platforms, and with professional advisers or authorities where the law requires it. Every provider we use is required to protect your data.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">6. How long we keep it</h2>
          <p>We keep quote enquiries for up to 12 months from our last contact with you. If you become a customer, we keep records of your installation and support history for as long as you remain a customer and for 6 years afterwards to meet our legal and warranty obligations. Marketing preferences are kept until you unsubscribe.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">7. How we protect it</h2>
          <p>Your information is stored on secured systems with access limited to the people who need it to serve you. We use reputable providers, keep software up to date and never store more information than we need.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">8. Your rights</h2>
          <p>Under UK data protection law you have the right to access a copy of your personal data, to have inaccurate data corrected, to have your data deleted, to object to or restrict our processing, to data portability, and to withdraw consent at any time. To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:contact@suttonss.co.uk" class="text-brand underline">contact@suttonss.co.uk</a>. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" class="text-brand underline">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">9. Cookies</h2>
          <p>This website uses only the cookies necessary for it to function and does not use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies. If we introduce analytics in future, we will update this policy and ask for your consent where required.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">10. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be published on this page with the date it was last revised.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
